data: {"sequence":13,"event_type":"escalated","actor":"Professor","message":"Review cap reached; the result is NOT signed off.","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:07:37.458153+00:00","data":{"report":{"case_id":"etch_bosch_trench_v1","summary":"Completed 3 review round(s); escalated to a human.","figures":[],"calibration":{"gaps":[],"tuned_parameters":{},"converged":false},"reviews":[{"verdict":"revise","round":1,"rubric_results":[{"item_id":"te_range","status":"pass","value":"min=1.87 max=1.87","expected":"1 .. 10 eV"},{"item_id":"ne_range","status":"pass","value":"min=3.96e+17 max=6.4e+17","expected":"1e+15 .. 1e+19 m^-3"},{"item_id":"ion_flux_range","status":"pass","value":"min=7.92e+19 max=1.28e+20","expected":"1e+18 .. 1e+21 m^-2 s^-1"},{"item_id":"power_balance_residual","status":"pass","value":"min=1e-12 max=1e-12","expected":"|x| <= 10 %"},{"item_id":"etch_rate_magnitude","status":"warn","value":"absent","expected":"Etch rate magnitude plausible for Si in fluorine chemistry"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=1.28e+20, n0*u_B=1.36e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=1.11e+20, n0*u_B=1.18e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=9.78e+19, n0*u_B=1.04e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=8.75e+19, n0*u_B=9.3e+20, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=7.92e+19, n0*u_B=8.41e+20, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"}],"physics_checks":[{"name":"electron temperature in a low-pressure ICP global model","status":"warn","detail":"Literature-derived check: validate against the cited passage. Question: electron temperature in a low-pressure ICP global model.","citation":"Kimura et al. (2002). Model and probe measurements of inductively coupled CF4 discharges, Journal of Applied Physics. PDF p. 2."},{"name":"Bohm flux at a plasma wafer sheath edge","status":"warn","detail":"Literature-derived check: validate against the cited passage. Question: Bohm flux at a plasma wafer sheath edge.","citation":"Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005). Principles of Plasma Discharges and Materials Processing, 2nd ed. pp. 173-174, PDF pp. 210-211."},{"name":"CF4/O2 ICP silicon etch rate versus substrate bias","status":"warn","detail":"Literature-derived check: validate against the cited passage. Question: CF4/O2 ICP silicon etch rate versus substrate bias.","citation":"COMSOL App. Library (CF4/O2 ICP). Model of a CF4/O2 Inductively Coupled Plasma Reactor with RF Bias for Silicon Etching (Application Library model, COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4). PDF p. 6."}],"feedback":["Rubric failure: `species_densities_positive` failed across all points because `species_m3` is completely empty. The simulation output must populate positive, finite densities for all active plasma species.","Fundamental problem scope mismatch: The user question requests planning a Bosch deep-silicon trench and reporting depth, CD, and sidewall profile using an SF6/C4F8 recipe (800 W, 50 mTorr, 120 cycles, target depth 80 um, CD 5 um). However, the plan executed an inert argon 0D plasma model (`chemistry_ar_lieberman.yaml`), omitting profile evolution entirely.","No etch rate, trench depth, critical dimension (CD), or sidewall scalloping profile was computed (`etch_rate_nm_per_min` is null). An appropriate feature-scale/Bosch trench solver (such as `viennaps_bosch`) and time-multiplexed etch/passivation chemistry must be utilized to address the question.","Calibration has not converged (`converged: false` with empty gaps against Kimura & Noto 2006). Calibration targets must align with the active chemistry and physical process under investigation."],"citations":["Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005). Principles of Plasma Discharges and Materials Processing, 2nd ed. pp. 173-174, PDF pp. 210-211.","Chen et al. (2002). Effect of process parameters on the surface morphology and mechanical performance of silicon structures after deep reactive ion etching (DRIE), Journal of Microelectromechanical Systems. PDF pp. 1-2.","Boer et al. (2002). Guidelines for etching silicon MEMS structures using fluorine high-density plasmas at cryogenic temperatures, Journal of Microelectromechanical Systems. PDF pp. 1-2.","Kimura et al. (2002). Model and probe measurements of inductively coupled CF4 discharges, Journal of Applied Physics. PDF p. 2.","COMSOL App. Library (CF4/O2 ICP). Model of a CF4/O2 Inductively Coupled Plasma Reactor with RF Bias for Silicon Etching (Application Library model, COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4). PDF p. 6."]},{"verdict":"revise","round":2,"rubric_results":[{"item_id":"te_range","status":"pass","value":"min=1.87 max=1.87","expected":"1 .. 10 eV"},{"item_id":"ne_range","status":"pass","value":"min=3.96e+17 max=6.4e+17","expected":"1e+15 .. 1e+19 m^-3"},{"item_id":"ion_flux_range","status":"pass","value":"min=7.92e+19 max=1.28e+20","expected":"1e+18 .. 1e+21 m^-2 s^-1"},{"item_id":"power_balance_residual","status":"pass","value":"min=1e-12 max=1e-12","expected":"|x| <= 10 %"},{"item_id":"etch_rate_magnitude","status":"warn","value":"absent","expected":"Etch rate magnitude plausible for Si in fluorine chemistry"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=1.28e+20, n0*u_B=1.36e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=1.11e+20, n0*u_B=1.18e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=9.78e+19, n0*u_B=1.04e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=8.75e+19, n0*u_B=9.3e+20, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=7.92e+19, n0*u_B=8.41e+20, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"}],"physics_checks":[{"name":"electron temperature in a low-pressure ICP global model","status":"pass","detail":"Te = 1.87 eV is physically plausible for an argon ICP at 50 mTorr given particle balance, though unrepresentative of an SF6/C4F8 electronegative Bosch discharge.","citation":"Kimura et al. (2002). Model and probe measurements of inductively coupled CF4 discharges, Journal of Applied Physics. PDF p. 2."},{"name":"Bohm flux at a plasma wafer sheath edge","status":"pass","detail":"Edge-to-center sheath density ratio h ~ 0.094 conforms to the intermediate-pressure heuristic h_L, h_R in Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005) pp. 173-174.","citation":"Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005). Principles of Plasma Discharges and Materials Processing, 2nd ed. pp. 173-174, PDF pp. 210-211."},{"name":"CF4/O2 ICP silicon etch rate versus substrate bias","status":"fail","detail":"No silicon etch rate or profile evolution was simulated; pure argon global modeling cannot address the deep reactive ion etching (DRIE) trench depth, CD, and scalloping requirements.","citation":"COMSOL App. Library (CF4/O2 ICP). Model of a CF4/O2 Inductively Coupled Plasma Reactor with RF Bias for Silicon Etching (Application Library model, COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4). PDF p. 6."}],"feedback":["Rubric check `species_densities_positive` failed across all points because `species_m3` is completely empty. The simulation output must populate non-empty, finite, positive densities for all active plasma species.","Fundamental physics and scope mismatch: The task specifies planning a Bosch deep-silicon trench and reporting depth, CD, and sidewall profile using SF6/C4F8 (800 W, 50 mTorr, 120 cycles, target depth 80 um, CD 5 um). The simulation substituted an inert argon 0D plasma model (`chemistry_ar_lieberman.yaml`), failing to model the chemical etching, passivation cycles, or profile evolution.","No etch rate, trench depth, critical dimension (CD), or sidewall profile was computed (`etch_rate_nm_per_min` is null). The workflow must employ a feature-scale Bosch profile solver (e.g., `viennaps_bosch`) coupled to appropriate etch/deposition parameters.","Calibration has not converged (`converged: false` with empty gaps against Kimura & Noto 2006). Calibration targets must match the active chemistry and physical quantities under investigation."],"citations":["Kimura et al. (2002). Model and probe measurements of inductively coupled CF4 discharges, Journal of Applied Physics. PDF p. 2.","Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005). Principles of Plasma Discharges and Materials Processing, 2nd ed. pp. 173-174, PDF pp. 210-211.","COMSOL App. Library (CF4/O2 ICP). Model of a CF4/O2 Inductively Coupled Plasma Reactor with RF Bias for Silicon Etching (Application Library model, COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4). PDF p. 6."]},{"verdict":"escalate","round":3,"rubric_results":[{"item_id":"te_range","status":"pass","value":"min=1.87 max=1.87","expected":"1 .. 10 eV"},{"item_id":"ne_range","status":"pass","value":"min=3.96e+17 max=6.4e+17","expected":"1e+15 .. 1e+19 m^-3"},{"item_id":"ion_flux_range","status":"pass","value":"min=7.92e+19 max=1.28e+20","expected":"1e+18 .. 1e+21 m^-2 s^-1"},{"item_id":"power_balance_residual","status":"pass","value":"min=1e-12 max=1e-12","expected":"|x| <= 10 %"},{"item_id":"etch_rate_magnitude","status":"warn","value":"absent","expected":"Etch rate magnitude plausible for Si in fluorine chemistry"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=1.28e+20, n0*u_B=1.36e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=1.11e+20, n0*u_B=1.18e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=9.78e+19, n0*u_B=1.04e+21, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=8.75e+19, n0*u_B=9.3e+20, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"bohm_flux_consistency","status":"pass","value":"reported=7.92e+19, n0*u_B=8.41e+20, h=0.0941","expected":"h = Gamma/(n0*u_B) within 0.04-1.08"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"},{"item_id":"species_densities_positive","status":"fail","value":"none","expected":"non-empty; all densities > 0 and finite"}],"physics_checks":[{"name":"electron temperature in a low-pressure ICP global model","status":"warn","detail":"Te = 1.87 eV is consistent with electropositive argon ICP particle balance at 50 mTorr, but unrepresentative of electronegative SF6/C4F8 Bosch process chemistry.","citation":"Kimura et al. (2002). Model and probe measurements of inductively coupled CF4 discharges, Journal of Applied Physics. PDF p. 2."},{"name":"Bohm flux at a plasma wafer sheath edge","status":"pass","detail":"Sheath edge density ratio h = Gamma / (n0 * u_B) = 0.0941 is physically consistent with intermediate-pressure Lieberman Bohm edge factors (h_L, h_R).","citation":"Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005). Principles of Plasma Discharges and Materials Processing, 2nd ed. pp. 173-174, PDF pp. 210-211."},{"name":"CF4/O2 ICP silicon etch rate versus substrate bias","status":"fail","detail":"Etch rate and etchant fluxes are completely absent/null across all bias points. Profile evolution and silicon etching metrics are not computed.","citation":"COMSOL App. Library (CF4/O2 ICP). Model of a CF4/O2 Inductively Coupled Plasma Reactor with RF Bias for Silicon Etching (Application Library model, COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4). PDF p. 6."}],"feedback":["Rubric check `species_densities_positive` failed across all bias points because `species_m3` is completely empty. The solver must populate non-empty, finite, positive number densities for all active plasma species.","Fundamental process chemistry mismatch: The recipe specifies Bosch deep reactive-ion etching of silicon using SF6/C4F8 (800 W, 50 mTorr, 120 cycles, target trench depth 80 um, CD 5 um). Simulating an electropositive pure argon plasma (`chemistry_ar_lieberman.yaml`) with zero flow fails to represent the chemical etching and polymer passivation kinetics of the Bosch process.","Missing feature-scale simulation and metrics: The prompt asks for trench depth, CD, and sidewall profile. Running only `plasma_global_model` with `etch_rate_nm_per_min: null` cannot address feature profile evolution. The plan must incorporate a feature profile solver (such as `viennaps_bosch`) coupled to realistic etch/passivation fluxes.","Incomplete calibration: Calibration targets remain unconverged (`converged: false`) with no reported gaps against empirical benchmarks. Ensure calibration quantities and chemistry match the actual process.","Review cap of 3 reached; ESCALATED \u2014 NOT SIGNED OFF."],"citations":["Lieberman & Lichtenberg (2005). Principles of Plasma Discharges and Materials Processing, 2nd ed. pp. 173-174, PDF pp. 210-211.","Kimura et al. (2002). Model and probe measurements of inductively coupled CF4 discharges, Journal of Applied Physics. PDF p. 2.","COMSOL App. Library (CF4/O2 ICP). Model of a CF4/O2 Inductively Coupled Plasma Reactor with RF Bias for Silicon Etching (Application Library model, COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4). PDF p. 6."]}],"open_issues":["Review cap reached; result is not signed off."],"sign_off":"escalated","signed_off_by":null}}}

